      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The answer is in [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into that environment in the first place.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent or Query agent), immediately before those processes start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the credential\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the Anthropic API key simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
